 unscored. Runs live under `runs/wb/<subset>/`.
 
 For Codex, start the bridge with `harness2-bridge --host 0.0.0.0` so that the containers can reach it.
+
+## EntBench
+
+[EntBench](https://github.com/vsingh45/par-entbench) is an enterprise multi-agent
+workload: a Planner-as-Router planner splits each question into subtasks, picks a
+specialist and a model size for each, and six specialists (SQL, MongoDB, extraction,
+reconciliation, tool planning, policy) answer in JSON. Grading executes the generated
+SQL and MongoDB against live databases, so scores are exact, not model-judged. Task
+classes are the domains.
+
+Unlike the other cells, the executor is a fixed workflow rather than a coding agent:
+the harness is PaR's prompt set (planner, classifier, one `AGENT.md` per specialist,
+plus shared guardrails, tool guidance and memory). Skills, scripts and plugins are
+rejected. `--substrate` does not apply.
+
+Set up par-entbench on its `harness2-integration` branch, then point Harness² at it:
+
+```bash
+git clone -b harness2-integration https://github.com/vsingh45/par-entbench.git
+cd par-entbench && python -m venv .venv && .venv/bin/pip install -e . && docker compose up -d
+export ENTBENCH_REPO=$PWD ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=...
+export HARNESS2_IMPROVER_MODEL=anthropic/<model>   # the improver runs in OpenCode
+
+harness2-setup eb        # installs OpenCode for the improver
+harness2-check --bench eb
+harness2 --bench eb --k 1 --mode parallel --only-domains sql_gen --max-tasks 1
+harness2-judge --bench eb --k 1 --mode parallel
+```
+
+Rollouts run in the par-entbench environment through `python -m entbench.rollout`,
+which is the only code that reads task files: the improver sees the question and its
+inputs, never gold answers or grading hints, and rollouts are written ungraded.
+`ENTBENCH_ROUTER` (default `par`) selects the PaR router. Runs live under `runs/eb/`.
